WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.033
[Music] 

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:09.060
[Andrew Ng] Today people are entering AI from all&nbsp;
walks of life and sometimes people still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:14.700
wonder is AI a right path for me.
[Fei-Fei Li] The truth is, if I could enter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:20.580
AI back then more than 20 years ago,&nbsp;
today anybody can enter AI because AI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:25.680
has become such a prevalent and&nbsp;
globally impactful technology.&nbsp;

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:29.340
[Andrew Ng] You actually started out not studying&nbsp;
computer science or AI but you started&nbsp;

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:34.440
out studying physics and so how did you&nbsp;
make that switch from physics to AI?&nbsp;

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:41.940
[Fei-Fei Li] Physics was my passion all the way through you&nbsp;
know middle school, high school, college, and one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:49.380
thing physics has taught me till today is really&nbsp;
the passion for asking big questions, the 

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:57.120
passion for seeking North Stars. And one thing I&nbsp;
did was reading up stories and writings of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:04.440
great physicists of the 20th century. It was really&nbsp;
interesting to notice that many of the writings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:10.980
towards the later half of the career of these&nbsp;
great physicists were not about just the physical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:20.580
world, but ponderings about equally audacious&nbsp;
questions like life, like intelligence, like human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:26.820
conditions. That really got me very curious about&nbsp;
the topic of intelligence. One thing led to another,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:34.560
during college time I did intern at a couple of&nbsp;
labs, especially vision related, and I was like wow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:43.080
this is just as audacious a question to ask as the&nbsp;
beginning of the universe or what is matter made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:52.380
of. And that got me to switch from undergraduate&nbsp;
degree in physics to graduate degree in AI. So I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.380 --> 00:02:00.366
think it is very exciting to be entering the science
of intelligence and and studying AI today. [Music]

